  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nShowers and thunderstorms will spread into the area as a cold front \napproaches and then drifts southeast across the area today into \nearly Saturday. Activity is then likely to continue -- at least \nacross the southeast half of the forecast area -- as the front \nstalls along the VA/NC border this weekend. \n\nAlthough some strong thunderstorms could occur in the vicinity of \nthe front today, mediocre lapse rates and instability should limit \nsevere weather potential. Conditions then generally remain \nunfavorable for severe weather through the weekend. Precipitable \nwater values in the 1.5 to 2 inch range are, however, expected to \nsupport heavy downpours at times.\n\nPrecipitation chances fade away early next week as a system \ntraverses eastern Canada and New England and propels the front \nfarther away from the area.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nCooler and quieter weather sets in for the new work week, with \npotential for temperatures to dip down into frost territory in the \nnortheast mountains early Tuesday and Wednesday mornings. \nTemperatures should then moderate for the second half of the work \nweek.",
